      "id": 5,
      "title": "Shards",
      "type": "Natural Law",
      "categoryId": 2,
      "summary": "When the United Being fractured, its pieces became shards: the powers standing behind the world's aspects, ranked from Time down to Nature Spirits. Mortals rarely meet a shard itself — only its power.",
      "body": "The fragments of the fractured [[United Being]] are called **shards**. Each shard is a being in its own right, with its own personality and its own goals for the world — and each one is the power behind some aspect of it.\n\n## A shard is not the thing it rules\n\nEvery fire burns by the power of [[Fire]], but no single flame is the Fire shard. Every breeze moves by the power of [[Air]], but the wind that hits your face is not the Air shard itself. The rock of the world's shell endures by the power of [[Libris]] - which is why the world bears that shard's name - but breaking a stone does not wound Libris, and dousing a flame does not diminish Fire. Mortals never touch a shard itself. They only ever deal with its power, which is everywhere its aspect is found.\n\nWhat sets a great shard above a small one is **scope**. An Element stands behind every instance of its kind in the world. A [[Nature Spirits|Nature Spirit]] stands behind one particular place — this mountain, this river, this forest — and aligns itself with the greater power whose aspect it shares.\n\nThe [[United Being]] created the world and souls. The [[Patrons|Patron]] shards gathered those souls and formed the races of the world in their own image. What remained of the United Being still rests at the core of the world as [[Equilibrium]], and it is the source of magic; the shards broke off from it.\n\n## The shards have a hierarchy\n\n| Rank | Shard |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | [[Time]]: the first shard to break away, and the only major shard. |\n| 2 | [[Light and Dark]]: Elements themselves, but so conjoined a pair that they are ranked together, above the other Elements — their power is combined. |\n| 3 | The [[Elements]]: [[Libris]], [[Air]], [[Water]], [[Fire]]. |\n| 4 | The [[Patrons]] of the races. |\n| 5 | [[Nature Spirits]]: minor shards that align themselves with the Elements, e.g. local mountains, rivers, forests. |\n\n## Not every shard became a power\n\nShards too small to influence anything were ejected into the cosmos and formed the stars; many conjoined to make the sun. This gestalt entity channels and directs the power from two shards; Fire and Light.",
